2
00:00:09,483 --> 00:00:13,998
The issue stays open, and the
customer is told it is unresolved.

3
00:00:14,038 --> 00:00:19,763
The engineer insists the fix shipped.
Support insists the tracker says otherwise.

4
00:00:19,803 --> 00:00:21,685
Your CTO asks: what failed?

5
00:00:22,025 --> 00:00:27,053
Nothing failed. The pull request didn't
target the default branch, and the keyword

6
00:00:27,093 --> 00:00:32,183
is interpreted only there. Two systems were
involved, text in one and a rule in the

7
00:00:32,223 --> 00:00:36,386
other, and each did exactly what it
documents. Hold on to issue 812.

8
00:00:36,426 --> 00:00:41,393
An issue can stay open for three reasons,
and you'll be able to name all of them.

